commit 12db4a7fbf22331bdd7f5ecfd9fe57067749a6f3
Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 06:39:20 2026 +1100

    Only inspect eventlet if it is already imported
    
    daemon.py imports eventlet at module level to find out whether it has
    been monkey patched. That import pulls in dnspython, cryptography and
    pyOpenSSL, which stay resident in every privsep daemon for about 20MB
    each. Look eventlet up in sys.modules instead.
    
    If nothing has imported eventlet it cannot have patched anything, so
    behaviour is unchanged. Unlike removing eventlet support entirely, this
    is safe to backport.
    
    Prompt: Mikal asked for oslo.privsep memory fixes that can be landed one
    at a time and measured in devstack CI; this is the minimal,
    behaviour-preserving alternative to the eventlet-removal change.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, low effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, low effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    Depends-On: https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/devstack/+/1011787
    Change-Id: Ic25f2a29380c349c5f87f4a74964bcffe42c4d8e
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

